-- title:
--   Multidegree zero forces algebraic equivalence to zero on fibres
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a package $\mathfrak{X}$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data over $\mathbb{Z}$ at $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ and a surjective ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$, together with a resolved model package $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}$ for these data, with total space $Y$, structure morphism $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, a morphism $\mathrm{toDR}$ to the base change $\mathfrak{X} \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec} O$, a finite set of nodes with widths $\mathrm{width}$, and invertible ideal sheaves $\mathrm{comp}\,c$ indexed by $c \in \mathrm{X0MqComponents}(\mathrm{width}) = \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_{n}\mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(n)-1)$, the components of the resolved special fibre. Given $m$ sections $\sigma_j : \operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ of $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}$'s structure morphism, natural numbers $\mathrm{pos}_j, \mathrm{neg}_j$, and components $v_j$ such that for each $j$ the specialisation $\sigma_j(\text{closed point})$ lies in $\mathfrak{X}_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{smoothOffEdges}$ and lies in the support of $\mathrm{comp}(v_j)$ and in no other $\mathrm{comp}(w)$; assume $\sum_j (\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j) = 0$, and that for vertical multiplicities $a^{+}, a^{-} : \mathrm{X0MqComponents}(\mathrm{width}) \to \mathbb{N}$ one has, for every component $c$, $$\sum_{j,\,v_j = c} (\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j) + \sum_{F} (a^{+}_F - a^{-}_F)\,\mathrm{inter}(F,c) = 0,$$ where $\mathrm{inter}$ is the intersection form of the table $\mathrm{x0MqResolvedTable}(\mathrm{width})$ (all multiplicities $1$; $\mathrm{inter}(i,j)$ the adjacency number for $i \neq j$, and minus the total adjacency degree on the diagonal). Let $M$ be a module on $\mathfrak{X} \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec} O$ that is invertible, i.e. locally isomorphic to the unit module, and suppose the pullback of $M$ along $\mathrm{toDR}$ is isomorphic to $$\bigotimes_{j}\Bigl(\bigl(\ker \sigma_j^{\,\mathrm{pos}_j}\bigr)^{\vee} \otimes \ker \sigma_j^{\,\mathrm{neg}_j}\Bigr) \otimes \Bigl(\textstyle\prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^{+}_F}\Bigr)^{\vee} \otimes \prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^{-}_F},$$ the tensor product being taken as an iterated right fold over $j = 0,\dots,m-1$, and where for an ideal sheaf $I$ the module $I.\mathrm{module}$ is the kernel of the map from the unit to the pushforward of the unit along the closed immersion of the associated subscheme, and $I.\mathrm{invModule}$ is its dual. Then for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ whose image contains the closed point of $O$, the pullback of $M$ to the geometric fibre $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{pullback.snd}, s)$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsAlgEquivZero}$ for the fibre morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} k$: there are a geometrically integral morphism $T' \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ locally of finite type, an invertible module on the product of the fibre with $T'$, and two $k$-points of $T'$ at which that module restricts to the structure sheaf and to the pullback of $M$ respectively.
--
--   This is the statement that a line bundle on a Deligne–Rapoport model which, after pullback to a regular resolved model, is cut out by a combination of horizontal sections and vertical components of multidegree zero on every component of the special fibre at $p$, has all its geometric fibres over the closed point algebraically equivalent to zero, i.e. in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$. It feeds the construction of $O$-sections of the relative Picard scheme from degree-zero divisor data, being cited by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective).
